DRAM and POST Troubleshooting

System: Desktop PC Workstation

Problem

The desktop powered on but would not complete POST and no video output came on

Troubleshooting steps taken:
Disconnected the AC power and discharged the system.
Removed the RAM stick from slot A2.
Powered the system on and checked the motherboard debug LEDs and speaker.
Noted the memory error shown by the motherboard.
Powered the system back down and checked the RAM and slot for visible damage or dirt, .
Fix
Reinstalled the RAM stick into slot A2.
Pressed down evenly until both retention clips locked into place.
Powered the system back on and allowed it to retrain the memory.
Result

The system completed POST and entered the UEFI setup screen with the expected amount of RAM detected.

